/*!
@defgroup etmr_ic_driver eTMR Input Capture Driver (eTMR_IC)
@ingroup etmr
@details
@brief Input capture mode driver for the eTMR peripheral.

## Overview

The IC (Input Capture) sub-module measures input signal timing
characteristics including period, positive pulse width, and negative
pulse width. It supports single-edge, dual-edge, and optional
hardware-accelerated capture modes.

## Features

- Rising, falling, or dual-edge capture
- Period measurement (using single or dual edges)
- Positive and negative pulse-width measurement
- Configurable input filter (sample counter and period)
- Per-channel DMA and interrupt support
- Combination capture mode (channel pair sharing)
- Hardware capture acceleration (device-dependent)

## Usage Pattern

@code{.c}
#define ETMR_INST (0U)

etmr_state_t state;
etmr_user_config_t config;

/* Step 1: Initialize common driver */
eTMR_DRV_GetDefaultConfig(&config);
eTMR_DRV_Init(ETMR_INST, &config, &state);

/* Step 2: Configure input capture */
etmr_ic_ch_param_t icChConfig = {
    .hwChannelId = 0U,
    .edge = eTMR_DUAL_EDGES,
    .measurementType = eTMR_PERIOD_MEASUREMENT,
    .filterSampleCounter = 4U,
    .filterSamplePeriod = 2U,
    .interruptEnable = true,
    .dmaEnable = false,
    .enableNotification = false,
    .channelsCallbacks = NULL,
    .channelsCallbacksParams = NULL,
};
etmr_ic_param_t icParam = {
    .numChannels = 1U,
    .countValue = 0xFFFFU,
    .inputChConfig = &icChConfig,
};
eTMR_DRV_InitInputCapture(ETMR_INST, &icParam);

/* Step 3: Wait for measurement to complete */
while (!eTMR_DRV_GetInputCaptureComplete(ETMR_INST, 0U)) {}

/* Step 4: Calculate and read results */
eTMR_DRV_CalculateChannelCaptureValue(ETMR_INST, 0U);
uint32_t period = eTMR_DRV_GetInputCaptureMeasurementPeriod(ETMR_INST, 0U);

/* Step 5: De-initialize */
eTMR_DRV_DeinitInputCapture(ETMR_INST, &icParam);
eTMR_DRV_Deinit(ETMR_INST);
@endcode

## API Quick Reference

### Initialization
| Function | Description |
|---|---|
| eTMR_DRV_InitInputCapture() | Configure channels in input capture mode. |
| eTMR_DRV_DeinitInputCapture() | Disable input capture and reset channels. |

### Measurement Query
| Function | Description |
|---|---|
| eTMR_DRV_GetInputCaptureComplete() | Check if measurement is complete. |
| eTMR_DRV_ClearInputCaptureComplete() | Clear the completion flag. |
| eTMR_DRV_GetInputCaptureMeasurementPeriod() | Get measured period. |
| eTMR_DRV_GetInputCapturePositivePulseCount() | Get positive pulse width. |
| eTMR_DRV_GetInputCaptureNegativePulseCount() | Get negative pulse width. |
| eTMR_DRV_GetInputCaptureValue() | Get raw CVAL register value. |

### Capture Processing
| Function | Description |
|---|---|
| eTMR_DRV_InputCaptureHandler() | Software capture interrupt handler. |
| eTMR_DRV_InputCaptureHardwareHandler() | Hardware capture interrupt handler. |
| eTMR_DRV_CalculateChannelCaptureValue() | Post-process captured timestamps. |

*/
